    "scenario": "BGP Attribute Router ID",
    "goals": "• All IP addresses have been preconfigured for you.\n• Router {{router1_name}}, {{router2_name}}, and {{router3_name}} already have the necessary BGP configuration for this task.\n  AS {{as1}}: {{router1_name}}\n  AS {{as2}}: {{router2_name}}\n  AS {{as3}}: {{router3_name}}\n  AS {{as4}}: {{router4_name}}\n• The loopback0 interface on router {{router1_name}} is already advertised in BGP.\n• Configure EBGP on router {{router4_name}} with its directly connected BGP neighbors.\n• Router {{router3_name}} should then have two paths to reach router {{router1_name}}'s loopback0 network.\n• Ensure router {{router3_name}} sends traffic to router {{router4_name}} to reach router {{router1_name}}'s loopback0 network. You are only allowed to make changes on router {{router4_name}}, and you must achieve this by configuring router {{router4_name}}'s BGP router ID.",
